{"bug":"K001","report":"B","v":"found","ref":"4. User-defined functions lose assignment overrides and cached values","evidence":"“line 241 creates an empty override map” and “the function sees the overridden assignment” identify the missing overrides and the resulting original value inside the function."}
{"bug":"K001","report":"D","v":"found","ref":"2. User-defined functions discard evaluated module state","evidence":"“fresh scope and empty override map at line 241”; invocation “x=changed recipe” prints “changed original”, identifying both the mechanism and ignored command-line override."}
{"bug":"K003","report":"D","v":"missed","ref":"Report-wide; finding 1","evidence":"“it removes `eager` from assignments and `[private]` from aliases and modules” concerns source formatting. The report never alleges backtick stdout losing trailing spaces or tabs."}
{"bug":"K004","report":"D","v":"missed","ref":"3. Modules sharing a source file share the wrong identity","evidence":"“compilation caches the contextual AST solely by file path” describes module identity conflation, not an AmbiguousModuleFile panic from unwrapping strip_prefix(parent) for an outside module path."}
{"bug":"K005","report":"B","v":"missed","ref":"6. Relative search ceilings are ignored","evidence":"“compares absolute search directories with an unnormalized ceiling” concerns search boundaries. The report does not identify unnormalized module paths, missed cycles through `..`, or repetition until the OS path limit."}
{"bug":"K009","report":"A","v":"partial","ref":"4. Invalid date/time formats panic","evidence":"“`datetime('%Q')`” and “`datetime_utc('%Q')`” terminate with “a Display implementation returned an error unexpectedly”. This identifies the invalid-format panics but does not identify format(...).to_string() on a fallible Chrono formatter as their cause."}
{"bug":"K010","report":"B","v":"found","ref":"5. Invalid datetime formats panic instead of returning errors","evidence":"“`--timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'`” exits 101; the finding cites src/config.rs:137 and explains that “`.to_string()` on Chrono formatting results” can encounter formatting errors."}
{"bug":"K010","report":"D","v":"found","ref":"4. Invalid datetime formats panic instead of returning errors","evidence":"The finding cites src/config.rs:137, states “converting Chrono’s failing `Display` implementation with `to_string()` panics”, and identifies “`--timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'`” as an input that exits 101."}
{"bug":"K011","report":"A","v":"partial","ref":"2. User-defined functions discard module variable state","evidence":"“With `y := 'global'; x := y; f(y) := x`, calling `f('parameter')` returns `parameter`, rather than `global`.” This identifies parameter interference with an assignment reference, but does not name the required scope-before-module-assignments lookup order."}
{"bug":"K011","report":"B","v":"missed","ref":"4. User-defined functions lose assignment overrides and cached values","evidence":"“creates a fresh root scope” and “creates an empty override map” describe lost function evaluation state. The report does not identify assignment references resolving to outer bindings because scope lookup precedes module assignments."}
